WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
Speaker 1: You know, we always say if only the&nbsp;
young people came out and voted, especially in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:14.040
midterms, look at what we could do. Well, we have&nbsp;
the numbers. 18 to 29 year olds saved the election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:24.060
last Tuesday. There is a really great explanation&nbsp;
from John Della Volpe. I hope I'm pronouncing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:35.760
correctly, where Dela Volpe explains the simple&nbsp;
math. Okay, high turnout combined with 63% of 18&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.660
to 29 year olds voting for Democrats versus 35%&nbsp;
of that very same group voting for Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:52.800
Gen Z and the younger millennials under 30&nbsp;
effectively canceled out every voter age 65 plus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:01.200
This is absolutely fascinating. And then when you&nbsp;
look at these groups, you look at 18 to 29 and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:10.200
look at 65 plus 18 to 29, had a plus three overall&nbsp;
contribution to the vote margin for Democrats and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:17.700
65 plus had a minus three overall contribution&nbsp;
for Democrats. We always talk about the older&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:23.700
generations are significantly more right leaning&nbsp;
and there's just not enough young people voting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:29.820
to cancel out or make up for that. That is exactly&nbsp;
what that is, literally what happened on November&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:38.880
8th. The very same three point contribution that&nbsp;
the 65 plus group overall made to Republicans was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:47.040
eliminated. It was zeroed out. It was tethered,&nbsp;
as we might say, by 18 to 29 year olds who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:53.100
contributed 80. Three point margin to Democrats.&nbsp;
It was their own future on the line. I wish that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:59.220
they would vote more, and it's important to focus&nbsp;
on the fact that it's not record breaking numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:06.000
